Link Qt6Core against the SDK's -lkandelo-mprotect on Kandelo.

io/qresource.cpp's mapUncompressed_sys() (compiled because musl defines
MREMAP_MAYMOVE and MREMAP_DONTUNMAP) remaps a resource and makes the copy
writable with mprotect(PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE). Kandelo's libc.a leaves
mprotect() out; -lkandelo-mprotect carries out requests that keep read
and write access, which is the only kind Qt6Core makes. As a private
library of a static Qt6Core it lands in Qt6CoreTargets.cmake as
$<LINK_ONLY:kandelo-mprotect>, so every CMake consumer links it without
naming it.

Justification: mprotect() is an explicit opt-in on Kandelo because
WebAssembly memory has no page protection (docs/sdk-guide.md, "Opt-in
libraries for unsupported APIs"). Qt6Core only asks to keep memory
readable and writable, which the truthful -lkandelo-mprotect carries
out, so linking it is the platform's intended path rather than a
workaround. Covered by qtgallery-smoke.

Exit: drop when Qt6Core no longer calls mprotect() on this path, or when
Kandelo's libc.a provides mprotect() by default.

--- a/src/corelib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/corelib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -804,6 +804,16 @@
     LIBRARIES
         fsnotify
 )
+
+# Kandelo (wasm32posix): io/qresource.cpp's mapUncompressed_sys() makes a
+# remapped resource writable with mprotect(PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE). Kandelo's
+# libc.a leaves mprotect() out; the SDK's -lkandelo-mprotect provides it,
+# carrying out requests that keep read and write access. A private library of
+# a static Qt6Core lands in its exported link interface, so every consumer
+# links it without naming it.
+if(LINUX AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^wasm(32|64)$")
+    qt_internal_extend_target(Core LIBRARIES kandelo-mprotect)
+endif()
 
 qt_internal_extend_target(Core CONDITION QT_FEATURE_qqnx_eventfd
     LIBRARIES
